From: =?UTF-8?q?K=C3=A9vin=20R=C3=A9mondi=C3=A8re?= <kevin@localhost>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 23:41:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 11/54] server: remove backend-sampling force-off for
 temp<=0.01 (MTP disabled)

The MTP-selective toggle forced backend-sampling OFF when temp<=0.01
(code path), which moved the entire sampling (top-k over 248k vocab)
back to CPU -> 90% CPU / freeze at 7 t/s. MTP draft removed from prod,
so this force is now harmful: code temp 0 must use backend-sampling
(GPU) like reasoning. Code temp 0: 25.5 -> 32.8 t/s.
---
 tools/server/server-context.cpp | 3 ---
 1 file changed, 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tools/server/server-context.cpp b/tools/server/server-context.cpp
index 5efbfc3854b..d54ad7c3f6d 100644
--- a/tools/server/server-context.cpp
+++ b/tools/server/server-context.cpp
@@ -1700,9 +1700,6 @@ private:
 
             bool use_backend_sampling = task.params.sampling.backend_sampling;
 
-            // le MTP sélectif désactive le backend-sampling (temp 0 = code)
-            use_backend_sampling &= !(task.params.sampling.temp <= 0.01f);
-
             // TODO: getting pre sampling logits is not yet supported with backend sampling
             use_backend_sampling &= !need_pre_sample_logits;
 
